# Set `version` to match the released tag once one is cut:
# version: 1.0.0
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: >-
    Component Trees of Pachner Graphs with Applications to Triangulated
    3-Spheres
  authors:
    - family-names: Faber
      given-names: Vance
      email: vance.faber@gmail.com
    - family-names: Murphy
      given-names: Michael
  year: 2026
  abstract: >-
    Fix a closed connected PL d-manifold M, where d >= 2. For each n, let G(n)
    be the graph whose vertices are the simplicial triangulations of M with n
    vertices, with an edge for each vertex-preserving bistellar flip, and let
    C(n) be its set of connected components. We form a directed graph of the
    components over all n, with an edge from U in C(n) to V in C(n+1) when a
    facet subdivision takes some triangulation in U to a triangulation in V.
    We prove that every vertex of this component graph has out-degree one, so
    that its underlying undirected graph is a graded tree, and derive
    canonical component paths, stabilization rays, and trunks. For S^3, the
    trunk contains every triangulated 3-sphere with at most 11 vertices, every
    12-vertex seed sphere with minimum edge valence at least 4, and every
    facet subdivision of each of the four known unflippable 3-spheres.
